 "cards": [
  {
   "dot": "cyan",
   "title": "Edge",
   "items": [
    "Caddy is never reachable directly from outside: every request and response, including the SPA bundle and the model files, passes the reverse proxy, which terminates TLS",
    "Any reverse proxy or tunnel works (the docs use a Cloudflare Tunnel); it talks plain HTTP to Caddy (auto_https off)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "dot": "violet",
   "title": "Frontend to backend",
   "items": [
    "Components never call the backend directly: they go through api/*.ts, one module per backend area, on a shared fetch wrapper (client.ts) that handles errors and session expiry",
    "The dashboard uses react-query for those calls; the public chat streams its reply via fetch POST to /public/{slug}/messages/stream",
    "Requests leave the browser through the reverse proxy and Caddy, which forwards /api to the backend"
   ]
  },
  {
   "dot": "amber",
   "title": "In the browser",
   "items": [
    "Speech recognition (Parakeet) and, optionally, speech output (Pocket TTS) run on the visitor's device",
    "Both load their model files from Caddy /models via the reverse proxy; the stt-model and tts-model download containers fill that directory",
    "Without the STT model the browser falls back to server-side transcription"
   ]
  },
  {
   "dot": "emerald",
   "title": "Core",
   "items": [
    "The backend owns the database, uploads, auth and the chat pipeline"
   ]
  },
  {
   "dot": "rose",
   "title": "Optional services",
   "items": [
    "tts-local, rag, rag-eval and docling start only with their Compose profile",
    "They publish no port; only the backend (and rag-eval to rag) calls them, with a shared token"
   ]
  }
 ]
}